---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PlotFigure from '../components/PlotFigure.astro';
import { LAB } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout title="Local files" wide>
  <div class="container wide full">
    <header class="head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Raw Slocum files</p>
      <h1>Read a glider’s own files, here.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Drop the flight and science files off a Slocum — <code>sbd</code>,
        <code>tbd</code>, <code>dbd</code>, <code>ebd</code>, <code>mbd</code>,
        <code>nbd</code> and their compressed twins — together with the
        <code>.cac</code> sensor lists they were written against. They are
        decoded in this tab and never leave your machine.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="drop" data-drop>
      <div class="zone" data-zone>
        <p><strong>Drop files here</strong>, or</p>
        <p class="picks">
          <label class="btn">
            Choose files
            <input type="file" multiple data-files hidden />
          </label>
          <label class="btn">
            Choose a folder
            {/* `webkitdirectory` is the only way to take a whole directory,
                and it is not in the HTML attribute types — set on the element
                at runtime instead of written here, which also keeps the
                type checker honest rather than silenced. */}
            <input type="file" multiple data-folder hidden />
          </label>
        </p>
        <p class="mono muted">Nothing is uploaded. There is no server to upload to.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="report" data-report></p>
      <div class="deployments" data-deployments hidden>
        <label>
          <span class="eyebrow">Deployment</span>
          <select class="field" data-deployment></select>
        </label>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div hidden data-panels>
      <section class="pair">
        <figure class="map-figure">
          <figcaption class="topline">
            <span class="eyebrow">Track</span>
            <span class="mono muted">coloured by time</span>
          </figcaption>
          <div class="map" data-map role="application" aria-label="Glider track"></div>
        </figure>
        <PlotFigure id="ts" title="T–S diagram" hint="Waiting for files…" />
      </section>

      <section class="sections">
        <h2>Sections</h2>
        <div class="chips" data-chips role="group" aria-label="Variables to plot"></div>
        <div data-figures></div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div hidden data-prototype-host>
      <PlotFigure id="prototype" title="Section" />
    </div>

    <details class="aside">
      <summary>What this does, and what it does not</summary>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The decoder is the one behind
          <a href={LAB.decoder}>oceansensing.org/data/slocum</a> — a
          from-scratch reader for Slocum’s dinkum binary format, validated
          against <code>dbdreader</code>. A Slocum file is <em>factored</em>:
          the sensor names live in a separate <code>.cac</code> file, so
          without the matching one a file is a list of numbers with nothing
          saying what they are. Drop the caches in alongside and they are
          remembered for next time.
        </p>
        <p>
          Seawater properties come from the same TEOS-10 implementation the
          deployment pages use, through the decoder’s own derivation — which
          matters here in a way it does not for the DAC: a Slocum writes
          conductivity in S/m and pressure in bar, and TEOS-10 wants mS/cm and
          dbar. Both are a factor of ten, and both are silent when wrong.
        </p>
        <p>
          Position needs the same care. A Slocum writes latitude and longitude
          as NMEA <code>DDDMM.MMMM</code>, which is a perfectly ordinary
          number — <code>3936.313</code> is 39.605° N, and read at face value
          it is a latitude that does not exist.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>No exports here.</strong> The decoder on oceansensing.org
          already writes CSV, netCDF-3 and OceanGliders OG1.0 from these same
          files, and is tested against a reference; a second implementation
          would be a second thing to keep correct. This page plots.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .head {
    margin-block: var(--space-xl) var(--space-lg);
  }

  h1 {
    margin-block: var(--space-2xs) var(--space-sm);
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: var(--prose-width);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .zone {
    border: 1px dashed var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-xl) var(--space-md);
    text-align: center;
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
  }

  .zone p {
    margin-block-end: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .picks {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .picks .btn {
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .report {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    white-space: pre-line;
  }

  .deployments {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-md);
  }

  .deployments label {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
    max-width: 32rem;
  }

  .pair {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    margin-block: var(--space-xl);
  }

  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .pair {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .map-figure {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .map {
    height: 30rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
  }

  .topline {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    margin-block-end: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>

<style is:global>
  [data-zone].over {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--bg);
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { startLocalPage } from '../lib/local-page';
  startLocalPage();
</script>
